.TH CJSON_LIST_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_list_remove \- remove and free an element from an array node by index
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cjson.h>

ccol_retval_t cjson_list_remove(cjson arr, size_t index);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes the element at position index from the array node arr and
recursively frees it together with all of its descendants.  All
elements after index are shifted left by one position (O(n) in the
number of elements after index).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - element removed and freed.
ccol_invalid_args   - arr is NULL, arr is not CJSON_LIST, or index is
                      out of bounds.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_list_push (3),
.BR cjson_list_get (3),
.BR cjson_dictionary_remove (3)
